  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper benchmarks five QAOA mixers (standard, XY-ring, XY-parity-ring, XY-full, QAMPA) on binary portfolio optimization instances built from German DAX-30 historical data (2016-2020), comparing noise-free statevector simulation against a 1000-shot qasm simulator. On n=10 assets with budget B=5 and QAOA depth p=7, the full-XY and QAMPA mixers achieve approximation ratio r>=0.98 and probability P~0.6 of recovering the brute-force optimum, while the standard mixer converges much more slowly; under measurement noise the XY-mixers become more sensitive than the standard mixer, so the best variant depends on device error levels.",
